{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977652748,"sessionID":"ses_1ccab6746ffesJigVqmjBVE5da","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_TNwasaQEyfSzCPVMuL3Lry8w","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"I was browsing the CL and found out there's an obsolete GO term dangling there. Not surprisingly, this is already an old issue. It might be an easy fix, so I'm bringing it to your attention again. \\n\\n> @dosumis opened this ticket last year about obsolete non-CL terms found in CL by reference check.\\n> \\n> I spotted another one by chance, and wonder if there are others:\\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> 'T follicular helper cell' Equivalent To 'CD4-positive helper T cell' and ('capable of' some GO_0051024)\\n> \\n> Where GO_0051024 is obsolete. In Protege it shows as strikethrough, but in [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/cl/terms?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCL_0002038) it doesn't, and in [Ontobee](http://www.ontobee.org/ontology/CL?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCL_0002038) it's only slightly more evident. \\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> In this case, the obsolete GO term has a replaced_by. Is there a way to trigger the replacement automatically, or at least to flag all instances of external classes that have OBO-compliant obsolete tags? Possibly run as a check with warnings (not errors) before each release? \\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> Tentatively assigning to @matentzn , though I see that this ticket is in the Icebox, and it's certainly not too urgent. \\n> \\n> Thanks!  \\n\\n _Originally posted by @paolaroncaglia in [#607](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/607#issuecomment-914349441)_\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-86eZP57\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"addiehl\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"Or just manually replace GO:0051024 with GO:0002639, which would be correct biologically.\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-02-13T18:29:41Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-2657418875\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     },\n19:     {\n20:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-869qXIK\",\n21:       \"author\": {\n22:         \"login\": \"github-actions\"\n23:       },\n24:       \"authorAssociation\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n25:       \"body\": \"This issue has not seen any activity in the past 6 months; it will be closed automatically in one year from now if no action is taken.\",\n26:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-13T02:43:24Z\",\n27:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n28:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n29:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n30:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n31:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3181998602\",\n32:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n33:     },\n34:     {\n35:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-869wHdY\",\n36:       \"author\": {\n37:         \"login\": \"dosumis\"\n38:       },\n39:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n40:       \"body\": \"Surely this should be checked at release time and flagged to be fixed\\r\\nbefore release.  Bit surprised this is not default ODK.  We used to have\\r\\nPerl scripts to prevent this during release.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn Wed, 13 Aug 2025, 11:43 github-actions[bot], ***@***.***>\\r\\nwrote:\\r\\n\\r\\n> *github-actions[bot]* left a comment (obophenotype/cell-ontology#2967)\\r\\n> <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3181998602>\\r\\n>\\r\\n> This issue has not seen any activity in the past 6 months; it will be\\r\\n> closed automatically in one year from now if no action is taken.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> —\\r\\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\\r\\n> <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3181998602>,\\r\\n> or unsubscribe\\r\\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAA3RR6QKGG3PZP4ODRIAOL3NKQ6FAVCNFSM6AAAAABXCZFORWVHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43OSLTON2WKQ3PNVWWK3TUHMZTCOBRHE4TQNRQGI>\\r\\n> .\\r\\n> You are receiving this because you were mentioned.Message ID:\\r\\n> ***@***.***>\\r\\n>\\r\\n\",\n41:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-13T11:52:17Z\",\n42:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n43:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n44:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n45:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n46:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3183507288\",\n47:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n48:     },\n49:     {\n50:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-86917R6\",\n51:       \"author\": {\n52:         \"login\": \"gouttegd\"\n53:       },\n54:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n55:       \"body\": \"Shouldn’t such cases be caught by ROBOT’s `deprecated_class_reference` standard report query?\",\n56:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-13T18:27:52Z\",\n57:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n58:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n59:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n60:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n61:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3185030266\",\n62:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n63:     },\n64:     {\n65:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-8692AIC\",\n66:       \"author\": {\n67:         \"login\": \"matentzn\"\n68:       },\n69:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n70:       \"body\": \"Exactly.\",\n71:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-13T18:34:33Z\",\n72:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n73:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n74:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n75:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n76:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3185050114\",\n77:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n78:     },\n79:     {\n80:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-8693KjQ\",\n81:       \"author\": {\n82:         \"login\": \"addiehl\"\n83:       },\n84:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n85:       \"body\": \"The specific fix for this term is to manually replace GO:0051024 with GO:0002639, which is correct biologically, and could have been done automatically using the 'term replaced by' annotation associated with GO:0051024.\",\n86:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-13T19:41:12Z\",\n87:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n88:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n89:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n90:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n91:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-3185354960\",\n92:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n93:     }\n94:   ],\n95:   \"title\": \"T follicular helper cell logical definition using obsolete term\",\n96:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967\"\n97: }\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"I was browsing the CL and found out there's an obsolete GO term dangling there. Not surprisingly, this is already an old issue. It might be an easy fix, so I'm bringing it to your attention again. \\n\\n> @dosumis opened this ticket last year about obsolete non-CL terms found in CL by reference check.\\n> \\n> I spotted another one by chance, and wonder if there are others:\\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> 'T follicular helper cell' Equivalent To 'CD4-positive helper T cell' and ('capable of' some GO_0051024)\\n> \\n> Where GO_0051024 is obsolete. In Protege it shows as strikethrough, but in [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/cl/terms?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCL_0002038) it doesn't, and in [Ontobee](http://www.ontobee.org/ontology/CL?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCL_0002038) it's only slightly more evident. \\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> In this case, the obsolete GO term has a replaced_by. Is there a way to trigger the replacement automatically, or at least to flag all instances of external classes that have OBO-compliant obsolete tags? Possibly run as a check with warnings (not errors) before each release? \\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> Tentatively assigning to @matentzn , though I see that this ticket is in the Icebox, and it's certainly not too urgent. \\n> \\n> Thanks!  \\n\\n _Originally posted by @paolaroncaglia in [#607](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/607#issuecomment-914349441)_\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-86eZP57\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"addiehl\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"Or just manually replace GO:0051024 with GO:0002639, which would be correct biologically.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-02-13T18:29:41Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2967#issuecomment-2657418875\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-869qXIK\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778977652705,"end":1778977652746}},"id":"prt_e3354bfd9001X4M4unsxao32fm","sessionID":"ses_1ccab6746ffesJigVqmjBVE5da","messageID":"msg_e3354ae81001uwoNtt391XIaDB"}}
